I walk into the large sports hall.
The light is very bright.
It is also very loud here.
People are playing badminton everywhere.
They run and jump on the courts.
I hold the racket in my hand.
I stop and watch.
The players on the court to the right are very fast.
They can hit the shuttlecock very hard.
I watch the games very closely.
I want to get on the court now too.
I walk a bit further.
Over there in the back, a court is still empty.
I stand next to the court.
Maybe other players will come soon.
Maybe I can play along then.
I gladly wait.
But my feet do not want to stand still.
I am ready for a game.
